Is there a bug in llvm, as the `conn_mss()` is returning `uint16_t` always so there should not be any warning.
The `conn_mss()` is specified as
```
#define conn_mss(_conn)					\
	((_conn)->recv_options.mss_found ?		\
	 (_conn)->recv_options.mss : (uint16_t)NET_IPV6_MTU)
```
and the type of `recv_options.mss` is
```
struct tcp_options {
	uint16_t mss;
	uint16_t window;
	bool mss_found : 1;
	bool wnd_found : 1;
};
```
